<mujoco model="sts3215">
  <!--
    Feetech STS3215 serial-bus servo: actuator model for the SO-101 arm joints.
    Identified parameters (BAM, model "m1"):
      kt               = 1.21164135295077      (torque constant)
      R                = 2.6761663274455603      (winding resistance)
      armature         = 0.02840336348682085
      friction_base    = 0.05239296084748866      (Coulomb / dry friction)
      friction_viscous = 0.05908515565091076
      q_offset         = -0.05116067663549731   (per-joint calibration zero offset, rad)

    MuJoCo mapping (class "sts3215"):
      joint.armature     = armature
      joint.frictionloss = friction_base                 (Coulomb)
      joint.damping      = friction_viscous + kt^2/R      (viscous + motor back-EMF)
                         = 0.05908515565091076 + 0.548574 = 0.607659
    The position actuator is the servo's internal position loop; kp/forcerange are the
    controller gain and torque limit (tune to taste; STS3215 stalls ~3 N-m).
    q_offset is a calibration offset (not applied here; the URDF uses the "new calib" zero).
    Include this file and tag the arm joints/actuators with  class="sts3215".
  -->
  <default>
    <default class="sts3215">
      <joint armature="0.0284034" damping="0.607659" frictionloss="0.0523930"/>
      <position kp="20" forcerange="-3.0 3.0"/>
    </default>
  </default>
</mujoco>
